      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(qa-lab): close transport before gateway teardown",
        "body": "Closes #106005\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nQA Smoke scenarios can finish successfully while Crabline transport work is still delivering an HTTP response. The suite stopped the gateway first, so that in-flight delivery became an unhandled `HTTP response closed before delivery completed` rejection.\n\nThe rebased branch also inherited a current-main architecture failure: the new read-only shared-state database boundary was missing from the raw SQLite guardrail allowlist.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nClose the transport before stopping the gateway. Transport cleanup drains outstanding provider HTTP work while the gateway can still accept delivery. The cleanup-order regression test preserves that ordering even when cleanup reports an error.\n\nAllowlist `openclaw-state-db-readonly.ts` alongside the existing state database lifecycle boundaries. It intentionally opens a read-only connection without joining writable schema repair, journal setup, checkpoints, or permission mutation.\n\n## User Impact\n\nQA Smoke no longer reports a post-success unhandled rejection caused by its own teardown order. Runtime behavior outside QA Lab is unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact-head architecture gate on `b0893f4203e7352d83f6c12c999be388a44abc3d`: passed, including Kysely guardrails and database-first legacy-store checks.\n- Exact-head focused QA extension suite: 29 passed.\n- Exact-head QA smoke on the QA Lab gateway plus `qa-channel` transport: `channel-chat-baseline` passed 1/1; output reached `CRABBOX_PHASE:complete` with `TEARDOWN_REJECTION:absent`.\n- Remote proof ran from content-verified source synced to DigitalOcean Crabbox (`provider=digitalocean`, lease `cbx_16a7892bd40b`, Node 24.18, public networking, Tailscale disabled); the lease was deleted after validation.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- Fresh autoreview reported no accepted or actionable findings.\n\n## Limitations\n\nThe full extension test-type project was not green locally because current main had unrelated iMessage nullability errors during the initial repair. The exact-head remote proof above covers this PR's changed behavior and the CI failure repaired here.\n\nAI-assisted: yes. No agent transcript attached (not requested).\n",
